{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/RESULT.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Citation-only judge version: build and $0 test result (D714)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Verdict:** judging-v12 and poc-v121 are built, and every registered $0 check passes (DESIGN.md §5, registered before the runs;\n     4\tD713). No paid call was made. Provider acceptance of the format, and whether the judge then picks the intended source, remain for\n     5\ta paid step that is Alex's to open (D712).\n     6\t\n     7\t## What was built (uncommitted)\n     8\t\n     9\t| File | Change |\n    10\t|---|---|\n    11\t| `src/hivemind/views/judging.py` | `judging-v12` added to `SUPPORTED_VERSIONS`, plus `CLOSED_LISTS` |\n    12\t| | `schema_for(version, lists)` closes the four id fields for v12: one shared `$defs` evidence enum, plain dependency and theme enums, `maxItems: 0` when a list is empty |\n    13\t| | `request_parts` returns the texts and the lists from the same rows; `build_prompt` delegates to it |\n    14\t| | `check_answer(..., lists)` checks membership against the lists under v12 |\n    15\t| | `round_of_judgements` sends each v12 view its own format, the retry included; v7/v8 still go through `build_prompt` with the frozen format |\n    16\t| `src/hivemind/model.py` | `check_schema` enforces `maxItems` |\n    17\t| `src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v12.txt` | a byte copy of judging-v7 (sha `d499c4b8…`) |\n    18\t| `poc/config/poc-v121.json` | poc-v118 with `rejudging.prompt_version` = judging-v12 |\n    19\t| `scripts/preflight.py` | part A checks judge rows against their saved format; a judge row without one fails `main` with exit 1 |\n    20\t| `tests/test_citation_lists.py` | 8 tests: T1c, T3, T3b, T5 and the format-error path |\n    21\t| `tests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py` | the v12 prompt and two v12 formats pinned; the v7/v8 format sha unchanged |\n    22\t| `tests/test_live_lock.py` | part A's stub returns the new pair |\n    23\t\n    24\t**Checks of the build**\n    25\t- Suite: 388 passed.\n    26\t- Mutants: 11 of 11 caught, each by its own assertion (`mutants.log`; the failing assertion of each was read).\n    27\t\n    28\t## The registered $0 checks\n    29\t\n    30\t| Check | Result | Record |\n    31\t|---|---|---|\n    32\t| **T1** old-2 replayed under poc-v121 | **PASS** | `poc/data/citation-t1-2026-11-21-run2/t1-result.json`, `t1-replay.log` |\n    33\t| **T1b** the four refused originals | **PASS** | same file |\n    34\t| **T1c** a real v12 retry | **PASS** | `tests/test_citation_lists.py` |\n    35\t| **T2** every stored shape, offline | **PASS** | `t2-result.json`, `t2-offline.log` |\n    36\t| **T3** the real validator's controls | **PASS** | `tests/test_citation_lists.py` |\n    37\t| **T3b** one owner of membership | **PASS** | same |\n    38\t| **T4** sizes | printed | `t2-result.json` |\n    39\t| **T5** preflight on a judge row without a format | **PASS** | `tests/test_citation_lists.py`; on old-2's real archive, part A checks its 4 refused judge rows against their saved format and preflight ends `preflight done` (`preflight-old2.log`) |\n    40\t\n    41\t### T1, old-2 replayed under poc-v121\n    42\t- 1,616 judge responses went through the transport, 4 of them labelled substitutions: 591→596, 6955→6979, 7068→7073, 7774→7780.\n    43\t- Every request equals old-2's outside the format.\n    44\t- Every format is strict, named `judgement`, and differs from judging-v7's only in the four constraints.\n    45\t- 0 list mismatches against the ids the text shows.\n    46\t- The store equals old-2's on all 36 shared tables, apart from the named columns:\n    47\t  - timestamps: `days_completed.at`, `processing_steps.at`, `views.created_at`;\n    48\t  - the judgements' `call_id`, `request_sha256` and `config_checksum`.\n    49\t- Positive control: one judgement's `why_changed` changed in a copy is reported as different.\n    50\t\n    51\t### T1b, the four refused originals\n    52\tEach goes through the real `model.call` under its v12 request and raises `SchemaError` on the id the check had refused: `e88`,\n    53\t`e3955`, `v10`, `e3998`.\n    54\t\n    55\t### T1c, a real v12 retry\n    56\tThe retry carries the first request's exact format and lists, plus the note.\n    57\t\n    58\t### T2, every stored shape\n    59\t- Population: 5,415 rows; 5,408 distinct pairs; 5,389 committed; 17 refused; 2 valid uncommitted.\n    60\t- Every committed and every valid uncommitted answer validates.\n    61\t- Every refused answer fails on its bad id:\n    62\t  - e362, e3111, e393;\n    63\t  - e88, e3955, e3998, e1382, e2769, e693;\n    64\t  - theme ids in cites (`v6`, `v10`);\n    65\t  - the dependency `v14` as evidence;\n    66\t  - `v5` in `cites_views`, four times.\n    67\t\n    68\t### T3, the real validator's controls\n    69\tIn all four fields, an allowed id passes and an unlisted id fails. An empty list allows only `[]`, and a correctly typed item fails\n    70\ton length.\n    71\t\n    72\t### T3b, one owner of membership\n    73\t- With a footnote in a quote, the v12 lists and the check accept the later real id.\n    74\t- v7's text parser refuses it. That narrowing is a latent defect of the frozen versions, recorded and not fixed there.\n    75\t\n    76\t### T4, sizes\n    77\t- Over the five archives the largest request has 451 evidence ids: 464 enum values with the shared enum counted once, 915 counted per\n    78\t  reference; 5,225 characters.\n    79\t- In the sealed D358 run the largest has 647 ids: 676 counted once, 1,323 per reference. 10 of 949 requests exceed the documented\n    80\t  1,000 if the provider counts per reference; none if it counts once.\n    81\t\n    82\t### Format size\n    83\tjudging-v7's format is 1,031 characters; v12's median is 1,396–1,405 and its max 5,225. At $0.10 per million input tokens this is\n    84\tnegligible.\n    85\t\n    86\t## Deviations, disclosed\n    87\t\n    88\t- **T1's first run** (`poc/data/citation-t1-2026-11-21/`) completed the replay, but the comparison crashed: a harness defect, since\n    89\t  FTS tables have no rowid. The transport's log was lost with it.\n    90\t  - The fixed comparison on that store found three differences. Each was named only after it was seen:\n    91\t    - `views.created_at`, a wall-clock timestamp;\n    92\t    - `link_selections`, a table the current uncommitted store schema adds (D694), empty;\n    93\t    - `dependencies.kind`, a column the same schema adds, on a table empty in both.\n    94\t  - The design's named class was \"timestamps … and new empty tables\". The added column on an empty table is the same kind, but not\n    95\t    named in advance.\n    96\t  - T1 was then rerun in full into `citation-t1-2026-11-21-run2/` and passed.\n    97\t- **The first harness's store** is left in place, marked harness-only.\n    98\t\n    99\t## What the $0 test cannot show (DESIGN.md §6)\n   100\t\n   101\t- Whether the provider accepts the exact format: the shared reference, `maxItems: 0`, and the largest request.\n   102\t- How the provider counts a referenced enum.\n   103\t- Whether the judge, constrained, cites the intended source (e3111 could become e3110 or e3112).\n   104\t- Whether forecasts move.\n   105\t\n   106\tA paid step answers these, and it is Alex's to open. Its first part would send the largest stored request and an empty-list request\n   107\tto check acceptance. Then it would re-send the 17 stored refused requests and a matched set of accepted ones under v12, and read the\n   108\tcited sources beside the forecasts.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '138,265p' docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md\"","aggregated_output":"| The input size | cost | about 450 characters at the median, up to about 3,700 at the five archives' max with the shared enum; priced at $0.10 per million input tokens; measured in the $0 test |\n\n### 4.3 New path × old checks\n\n| Old check | Under v12 |\n|---|---|\n| `check_answer` membership | under v12, checked against the same lists as the format, so it cannot fire on an answer that passed; v7/v8 unchanged |\n| Rung range, first-judgement changed, rung move needs changed, stance non-empty, duplicate theme push | unchanged |\n| Frozen tests | v7/v8 unchanged; v12's prompt sha = v7's; a pinned schema on a fixed list |\n| D359 (only named versions are built) | `SUPPORTED_VERSIONS` gains `judging-v12` only |\n| Launchers | poc-v121 is a product config like poc-v118 |\n\n### 4.4 Prior decisions\n\n- D354 and D712: the frozen judge, now opened by Alex.\n- D359: the code builds only named versions.\n- D694: a new name for a request change.\n- D198: the closed set is what the request showed.\n- D358: the evidence-bloat halts, the same class.\n- D711: the census and the recommendation.\n- The pre-v74i extraction admission schema constrained `folds_into` to the shown ids. It was removed with the frozen prompt (commit\n  248ef1b4); no decision rejected it.\n\n## 5. The $0 test (registered before it runs)\n\n### T1: the product path\nold-2 is replayed under poc-v121 through `replay.run`, serial path.\n- **The archive.** A scratch archive seeded with old-2's non-judge calls only, so every judge request misses it and reaches the\n  transport and the real validator.\n- **The transport.**\n  - It finds each judge request's stored old-2 call by its (system, user) bytes; the 1,620 pairs are unique (Codex r38).\n  - It asserts that the outgoing request equals the stored one in every key except the format.\n  - It asserts that the format has `strict: true` and the name `judgement`, and differs from v7's only in the four citation\n    constraints and the `$defs` they use.\n  - It asserts that each of the outgoing lists (evidence, dependencies, themes) equals the ids the request shows, read from its text\n    (evidence and theme entries; dependency entries).\n    - A mismatch is listed with its call and read by hand: a parser case is told from a builder bug before T1 can pass.\n    - An extra or missing id in any list fails T1. Codex r38c added an unlisted theme to 1,471 formats and every stored answer still\n      validated, so validation alone cannot catch it.\n  - It returns the stored answer, which goes through the real `model.call` and `model.check_schema`.\n  - Any other request (a non-judge miss, an unknown pair) stops the replay.\n- **The four refused first calls** (e88, e3955, e3998, theme ids). Each gets the saved accepted retry answer, labelled as a\n  substitution: under strict mode the provider could not have returned the refused one. All four retry answers fit their first\n  requests (Codex r38b). The four retry-note requests are not reached and are tested apart (T1b).\n- **Pass.**\n  - Exactly 1,616 judge responses through the transport, 4 of them labelled substitutions.\n  - The replay completes.\n  - The store equals old-2's on every table, listed explicitly from `sqlite_master`, with the expected differences named:\n    timestamps, archive call ids, request hashes, config checksum and version, and new empty tables.\n    - Judgements are compared on every substantive field: view, sequence, input, rung, reasons, reference, implied outcome, cites,\n      `cites_views`, pushes, theme pushes, changed, `why_changed`, publication day.\n    - Every other table is compared on all its columns but the named ones (handovers, match records, days completed and the rest).\n  - New request hashes and the config are checked apart.\n\nT1 does not touch provider acceptance (§6).\n\n### T1b: the four originals\nEach refused original goes through the real `model.call` under its v12 request and raises `SchemaError` on the id `check_answer`\nrefused.\n\n### T1c: a real v12 retry\n- A store fixture with a theme in force; a fake provider answers the first v12 request with a duplicate theme push, which\n  `check_answer` refuses, then answers the retry correctly.\n- Assert that the retry request carries exactly the first request's format, citation lists included, and the retry note.\n- Mutant: the retry sent with the open v7 format must fail this test.\n\n### T5: preflight on a judge row without a saved format\nA refused judge row whose request has no `response_format` makes `scripts/preflight.py` exit non-zero, with the row named.\nToday `main` ignores part A's result, so it also needs a failing exit for this case. Extraction and matching rows keep their\npaths.\n\n### T2: every stored shape, offline (evidence from archived text)\n- For every stored judge request of old-1, old-2, old-3, control-1 and linked-1, the lists are taken from the saved text. These are\n  archived calls whose store state is gone.\n- The parser can widen or narrow a list (the footnote case), so T2 is evidence from the archived text. T1 covers the built path.\n- Each answer is validated through the real `check_schema` with the v12 format.\n- Pass:\n  - all 5,389 committed answers and the 2 uncommitted valid ones validate;\n  - all 17 refused answers fail on their bad id;\n  - the population is printed as in §1.\n\n### T3: the real validator's controls\nFor all four fields, through `model.check_schema`:\n- an allowed id passes;\n- an unlisted id fails.\n\nAn empty list with `maxItems: 0` passes `[]`, and fails one otherwise valid item of the right type with an array-length error,\nnot a type error.\n\nT3 fails on today's validator, which ignores `maxItems`.\n\n### T3b: one owner of membership\n- A rendered request whose evidence quote holds a blank line followed by \"[1]\", with a real evidence entry after it. The v12 lists\n  include the later id, and `check_answer` under v12 accepts a citation of it.\n- The same answer under v7's text parser is refused. This control shows the parser case is real.\n\n### T4: sizes\nThe largest format over the five archives and over the sealed D358 archive is printed: evidence count, enum values with the\nreference counted once and counted twice, and characters.\n\n### Mutants\nEach is caught by a test that passes on the unmutated code:\n- push ids left open;\n- lists parsed from the text instead of taken from the rows (the multiline-quote case);\n- `check_answer` under v12 reading the text instead of the lists (T3b);\n- `maxItems` dropped for an empty list;\n- `maxItems` removed from the validator;\n- `strict` dropped from the outgoing format (T1);\n- preflight reading the fixed schema for judge rows.\n\n### Also\n- Prompt size: the format's characters and tokens before and after, median and max.\n- The suite, the frozen tests and `docs/check.py`.\n\n## 6. What the $0 test cannot show\n\n- **Provider acceptance of the exact format:** the shared reference, `maxItems: 0`, and a largest request (D358 call 6918's size).\n- **Whether the judge picks the intended source when constrained:** e3111 could become e3110 or e3112.\n- **Whether the forecasts move.**\n\nA paid step, Alex's to open, settles these. It would first send the largest stored request and an empty-list request to check\nacceptance, then re-send the stored refused requests and a matched set of accepted ones, and read the cited sources beside the\nforecasts.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D71[12]|citation|poc-v121' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md docs/DECISIONS.md | tail -n 30\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D71[12]|citation|poc-v121' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md docs/DECISIONS.md | tail -n 30\"","aggregated_output":"docs/CURRENT_STATE.md:75:Alex has authorized correcting the test-source cleaner and test data when their defects are confirmed, while the frozen production configuration and ruler remain intact. The cleaner switched 615 originally fed articles off; a replay reproduces all 615, and direct inspection confirms an actual article excluded because its 9,874-character body was flattened to one line. Other examples include a wrong-site shell, paywall and long challenge code, so the false-exclusion count and a general article-identification repair remain to be established. The [council regroup](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-REGROUP-COUNCIL.md) and [source-preservation design](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PRESERVATION-DESIGN.md) describe an isolated candidate checked against all 34,084 records, with a fake-answer actual-runner handoff and provenance display in the replay renderer. The [five source-control calls](../clean-arch/STEP1-CAPTURE-CONTROLS-RESULTS.md) completed and were source-reviewed; two items contain summary details absent from their attached quotations, and one source-visible risk explanation was not returned. This is selected-case evidence, not a general quality result. Broader source-quality comparison, citation completeness and actual writer integration remain open.\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:77:**Clean architecture Step 1 (2026-11-06, isolated work on `clean-arch`):** Alex reopened work with the clean architecture. An experimental prepared-source handoff now preserves the archived page, prior cleaned text, source-role decisions and selected-line mapping without changing the original database; quotations for prepared items must also occur contiguously in the original captured page. Two seven-item runs are available in the [clean architecture PRD](../clean-arch/PRD.md), one in the earlier selection order and one in recorded page-timestamp order. The source selector is not a production service and source ordering is not established event-arrival ordering. The runs expose unresolved semantic problems: citations can omit supporting facts despite an exact location match; model output can change a benchmark into a deployment, reverse a backup relation, omit a named customer or assign an unstated currency. A blinded 84-call check-placement/wording comparison and a 27-call same-article citation-completion diagnostic did not give a clean semantic fix and are not adopted. The latter missed an omitted connectivity condition and a reversed backup relationship, and left six expected evidence reviews unaddressed. A further five-round Codex–Claude council produced a narrowly scoped Step 1 link candidate, independently checked for prompt-contract drift. A six-article, 36-call blind comparison completed; the candidate still produced an explicitly self-contradictory link and both arms consistently omitted the same Kyber report and company response. It is not adopted and has not changed the active PRD prompt. A trace confirms that both the Kyber report and open Kyber thesis were supplied, and the raw model answers omitted the report and denial; the reason is not established. See ../poc/data/clean-step1-kyber-trace-2026-11-06/TRACE.md. An isolated six-call comparison showed that hiding the Kyber thesis did not recover the report or denial in any draw. A second six-call comparison returned them in 3/3 draws with the original Kyber paragraph alone and 0/3 with the full article; length, position and surrounding content changed together, so the reason is not isolated. Excerpt outputs have source-attribution limitations. Neither experiment changed state or established a production fix. (Superseded: the next task then was a whole-article coverage approach; the current next task is under \"One next task\".) See ../clean-arch/STEP1-IMPLEMENTATION-COUNCIL.md. The earlier four-round council agreed that no tested semantic fix is ready; its next investigation is a source-backed review of the 49-item historical run and its 160 evidence records, with overlapping issue flags and separate article-level omissions, then a separate comparison of the seven-item replays. See ../clean-arch/STEP1-COUNCIL-REVIEW.md. Preserve relevant evidence while identifying the next intervention; production/frozen history remains as described below. See [Step 1 run log](../clean-arch/STEP1-RUN-LOG.md) and [English reading page](../clean-arch/architecture.html).\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:124:**Clean Step 1 fidelity review (2026-11-07):** All 49 saved source packets and 160 original evidence items have received a source-and-record review; focused independent cross-checks cover the findings and selected controls. The [review and article replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-FIDELITY-REVIEW.md) distinguish source contamination and missing source material from model meaning, citation, date and link issues. The [isolated schema property-order diagnostic](../clean-arch/STEP1-CITATION-ORDER-RESULTS.md) completed all 66 calls and condition-blinded article reviews. Several omissions and semantic errors persisted; it did not establish a fix and is not adopted. It used saved articles and before-states without changing production.\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:448:**The one next task (D711, 2026-11-21): Alex's choice on opening a citation-only judge version** (closed per-request id lists in the\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:451:- **Verdict:** inconclusive (D711). control-1 stopped on 09-08 on a double refusal: two one-character evidence-id copy errors. linked-1\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:459:  - the citation-only version is the recommendation;\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:492:  passed review; the pilot ran at $1.70 and is inconclusive (D710, D711).\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:44:- **Citations.** D92's \"theme colours only\" is amended by D284 (plain blue citations).\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:628:| D284 | 2026-10-26 | Plain blue inline citations | in force | [frontend](DECISIONS-frontend.md) |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:1055:| D711 | 2026-11-21 | Pilot pair 1 inconclusive (control-1 double refusal on 09-08: two one-character evidence-id copy errors); the comparison closed, no redraw or resume (council round 37, consensus A). Exploratory beside it: Data Center never above total revenue in linked-1 (control-1 28 of 60 by parser, sampled dates real); four linked CPU double counts in total revenue (H4); H1 at the line (5 against 1). Recommended to Alex: a citation-only judge version with closed per-request id lists, tested at $0; the link direction designed separately | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PILOT-RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:1056:| D712 | 2026-11-21 | Alex opens a citation-only judge version (\"开引用格式新版本 (推荐)\"): every id field of the judge's answer takes a closed list built from the request; design, council, build, then a $0 test on stored data; any paid test asks Alex again | in force | `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:1057:| D713 | 2026-11-21 | Council R passes the citation-only judge design (round 38, four passes): judging-v12 = judging-v7 with closed per-request id lists from the rendered rows (shared evidence enum, maxItems 0 when empty), one owner of membership, validator maxItems, preflight on saved judge formats, poc-v121; build and the $0 test T1–T5 next | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md` |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
