{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n --glob '\"'!*.stream'\"' --glob '\"'!*.html'\"' '388 passed|docs/check.py|why_changed.*(mutat|copy|difference)|t1-replay.log' docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists; git diff -- src/hivemind/model.py\"","aggregated_output":"docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md:250:- The suite, the frozen tests and `docs/check.py`.\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/round39-brief.md:7:`docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/`: `mutants.py` (+ `mutants.log`), `t1_replay.py` (+ `t1-replay.log`), `t2_offline.py` (+\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/RESULT.md:25:- Suite: 388 passed.\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/RESULT.md:32:| **T1** old-2 replayed under poc-v121 | **PASS** | `poc/data/citation-t1-2026-11-21-run2/t1-result.json`, `t1-replay.log` |\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/RESULT.md:49:- Positive control: one judgement's `why_changed` changed in a copy is reported as different.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-1NAl5KOd' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-21 17:32:21.018 xcodebuild[23120:69625571]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-21 17:32:21.137 xcodebuild[23120:69625570] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-ntKd5Mtd' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-21 17:32:21.479 xcodebuild[23123:69625592]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-21 17:32:21.603 xcodebuild[23123:69625590] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ndiff --git a/src/hivemind/model.py b/src/hivemind/model.py\nindex 0415d765..1b326130 100644\n--- a/src/hivemind/model.py\n+++ b/src/hivemind/model.py\n@@ -183,7 +183,7 @@ def openai_transport(provider, request, timeout=180, max_attempts=3):   # the de\n \n def check_schema(value, schema, path='$', root=None):\n     \"\"\"A small validator for the subset of JSON Schema the prompts use: object/required/additionalProperties,\n-    array/items/minItems, string/enum/pattern, integer, number, boolean, null in anyOf, and $ref into the root's $defs.\"\"\"\n+    array/items/minItems/maxItems, string/enum/pattern, integer, number, boolean, null in anyOf, and $ref into the root's $defs.\"\"\"\n     root = root if root is not None else schema\n     if '$ref' in schema:\n         name = schema['$ref'].rsplit('/', 1)[1]\n@@ -220,6 +220,8 @@ def check_schema(value, schema, path='$', root=None):\n         errors = []\n         if len(value) < schema.get('minItems', 0):\n             errors.append(f'{path}: fewer than {schema[\"minItems\"]} items')\n+        if 'maxItems' in schema and len(value) > schema['maxItems']:\n+            errors.append(f'{path}: more than {schema[\"maxItems\"]} items')\n         for index, item in enumerate(value):\n             errors.extend(check_schema(item, schema.get('items', {}), f'{path}[{index}]', root))\n         return errors\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"git status --short -- docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists; sed -n '1,100p' docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/claude-r38.md\"","aggregated_output":"git: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-Rvwcbbxe' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-21 17:32:21.018 xcodebuild[23119:69625572]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-21 17:32:21.137 xcodebuild[23119:69625568] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-M985Q8om' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-21 17:32:21.479 xcodebuild[23124:69625591]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-21 17:32:21.603 xcodebuild[23124:69625589] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\n?? docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/\n# Claude's own reading of the design, round 38 (written before Codex's)\n\n- **T1's mechanics.** Under v9 every judge request has a new archive key. The product's `model.call` misses the scratch archive and\n  calls the harness transport. The transport finds old-2's answer by the system and user bytes, retry notes included.\n  - For old-2's 4 refused first answers it must return the stored refused answer anyway, so that `check_answer` refuses it, the\n    stored retry follows and the trajectory stays old-2's.\n  - It records that the answer fails the closed-list schema. A real provider could not have produced that answer under v9. The\n    replay keeps the old path so the stores stay comparable.\n- **The empty list.** `maxItems: 0` with `items: {\"type\": \"string\"}` avoids an empty enum, which the guide does not cover. A\n  schema-only check is still needed that the provider accepts `maxItems` under strict mode for this model. The guide says\n  `minItems`/`maxItems` are supported; it excludes them for fine-tuned models only.\n- **The provider's acceptance of the schema** cannot be shown at $0. The first send of a v9 request is the first proof. A schema\n  refusal is an HTTP 400 before generation, which the transport surfaces as an error (a resumable day), not a silent fallback. That\n  belongs in the later paid test's first step.\n- **Dependencies in v7's shape:** poc-v118 has no dependency rows, so `cites_views` is always `maxItems: 0` under poc-v121. In v8's\n  shape the block lists `- vN (` lines; the set must equal `check_answer`'s resolved dependencies (to verify on linked-1).\n- **Is the scope right?** Rung-range refusals were never observed; leaving the rung open follows \"no mechanism for an unnamed case\".\n- **Representation:** a plain enum per field fits every stored request (max 915 of 1,000). The margin is thin for a request showing\n  more than about 495 evidence ids; the refusal before the send makes that a visible failure, not a silent one.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
