{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT ACCEPT for handoff.** Preflight can report success when a refused judge record has neither a readable answer nor a saved answer format. I reproduced an exit of `0` for that case. The existing test supplies a readable answer, so it misses the early exit from the check. Check for the saved format first and add the malformed-answer case to T5. None of the reviewed archives contained that case. [Preflight](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/preflight.py:67) · [T5 test](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_citation_lists.py:147)\n\n**The judge build matches DESIGN v3.** v12 builds all four citation restrictions from the rows it shows and uses those same lists to check the answer. I exercised both older versions with a rejected citation. Each called `build_prompt`, rejected the citation in the existing answer check, and retried with the same open format. I found no v7 or v8 regression. [Judge round](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:369)\n\n**T1’s saved evidence holds.** I checked all 1,616 requests, the four labelled substitutions, the new request hashes and configuration, and the data in all 36 shared tables. Changing one saved explanation in memory made the comparison fail. The first comparison crash and the three differences named afterward do not undermine those findings. The timestamp fits the registered exception, the added table is empty, and the added column is on a table empty in both stores. The report omits a separate event. Run 2 saved passing T1 and T1b results, then exited `1` while printing its summary. The current summary code exits `0` with those saved results. Record both facts. The saved data is sufficient to verify the replay without repeating it. [Saved result](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/citation-t1-2026-11-21-run2/t1-result.json) · [Run log](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/t1-replay.log:43)\n\n**T2 and T4 reproduce.** Across 5,408 distinct request-answer pairs, all 5,391 valid answers passed and all 17 refused answers failed on unlisted IDs. The report’s shorthand omits that `v14` was used as evidence in two refused answers. Before saying *every registered $0 check passed*, supply the registered token counts and `docs/check.py` result, or state that they are outstanding. The reported character counts alone do not establish the cost claim. [Offline results](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/t2-result.json) · [Registered checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md:248)\n\nThe next test is the malformed judge record with no saved format. Once preflight names it and exits `1`, and the report reflects the evidence above, Alex can decide whether to authorize the paid provider check. This review changed no files and made no paid calls. The read-only sandbox prevented a fresh full-suite run."}}
